{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"EPIC PROGRESS — 6 of 8 stories CLOSED.\n\nCLOSED: J1 acb2, J2 62d9, J3 aac8, J4 0a94, J5 c97f, J6 9fd4.\nOPEN:   J7 b4e3 (plan review running), J8 8c35 (blocked by J7).\n\nJ6 closed CERTIFIED (plan-review + completion-verifier attestations, no --force-close). It took\nthree close attempts and five changes, because the completion verifier was RIGHT each time it\nrefused. It surfaced three production defects that would otherwise have shipped:\n 1. add_label called `add_field_value` on jira.JIRA — an attribute that does not exist (only\n    jira.resources.Issue has it, with a 2-arg signature). Every invocation raised: the DC\n    transport could never label an issue. It had no test at any tier.\n 2. _config_schema._validate_reconciler_tls — the control stopping a Jira PAT crossing the wire\n    in cleartext — had ZERO tests anywhere in the tree.\n 3. requests SSLError SUBCLASSES ConnectionError, so a TLS cert failure was retried as a\n    transient fault (3x, 2s+5s backoff) and surfaced without naming ca_bundle. Measured cost:\n    7.54s of pointless retry.\n\nEpic AC8 (record each story's merged Gerrit change) — J6's: 1049, 1053, 1055, 1069, 1071, 1082,\n1087. Epic-adjacent close-gate work: 1064 (d59e), 1073 (a89d instrumentation). 1060 ABANDONED."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785461757305307001,"uuid":"313e9c38-a30c-4187-9e47-b7b55c649514"}